rent in intervals[1:].\n3. Overlap condition: current[0] < last[1] excludes touching intervals. User specifically mentions touching intervals like [1,3] and [3,5]. Should they be merged? Usually merge overlapping intervals may or may not merge touching. The prompt says \"touching intervals like [1,3] and [3,5]\" as test case. It says merge overlapping intervals. Does touching count? In many LeetCode merge intervals, [1,4] and [4,5] merge because intervals are closed? Actually LeetCode: intervals [1,3], [2,6], [8,10] -> [1,6],[8,10]; [1,4], [4,5] -> [1,5] because they touch? It says merge overlapping intervals, but often if end equals start, merge. The test case", "top2": [[[1596, -0.0014672309625893831], [22916, -7.635134220123291]], [[1144, -1.1920935776288388e-06], [599, -14.367562294006348]], [[4087, -0.006704702973365784], [5707, -5.045237064361572]], [[1156, -0.0010838420130312443], [303, -6.963696002960205]], [[579, -0.5377994775772095], [13, -1.6299645900726318]], [[1622, -0.0034053425770252943], [9640, -6.822470188140869]], [[13, -0.008730683475732803], [25, -5.122574806213379]], [[14235, -0.06972979009151459], [26472, -3.512965202331543]], [[1423, -1.1122033596038818], [7936, -1.3329695463180542]], [[1396, -0.5321847200393677], [21851, -0.9665012955665588]], [[9584, -7.069360435707495e-05], [506, -10.160093307495117]], [[303, -0.25275319814682007], [11, -1.6206997632980347]], [[12654, -0.3748241066932678], [2574, -1.7872081995010376]], [[709, -0.10117249190807343], [10562, -2.353878974914551]], [[11, -0.47611376643180847], [10562, -1.5111384391784668]], [[10033, -0.0013085220707580447], [799, -6.932943344116211]], [[1754, -0.0013754286337643862], [799, -6.63223123550415]], [[303, -0.5684472918510437], [799, -0.8444444537162781]], [[799, -3.57628505298635e-06], [11316, -12.696416854858398]], [[11316, -1.1920935776288388e-06], [3106, -14.3519926071167]], [[11, -0.0056479028426110744], [13, -5.885169982910156]], [[2873, -0.5716903805732727], [1179, -1.16118705